  // response-shape-v1 + its first consumer rule (2026-08-03). The two bad routes declare DTOs whose
  // field names hit the sensitive vocabulary (substring `password`, suffix `token`) -> warning here
  // (nothing consumes them, which also co-fires unconsumed-endpoint on all four routes). The clean
  // interface-typed route and the undeclared-return-type route are negative controls for the rule
