  // NOT IN A FRESH CLONE -- this is the one expectation whose fixture file is deliberately absent from
  // the tracked tree, and it is listed in the `untracked` array at the bottom of this file so
  // benchmark.mjs can say so next to the FN it produces instead of leaving a red score unexplained.
  // `security/vendor-token-committed` only fires on a CONTIGUOUS live vendor-token literal, so its fixture
  // must contain the exact string shape that GitHub push protection rejects and that
  // scripts/check-vendor-token-literals.sh (no escape hatch, by design) blocks at commit time. Splitting
  // the literal was measured, not assumed: it silences BOTH rules on this line. Full reasoning and the two
  // ways out are in `.gitignore`, which is what actually excludes the file -- do not re-derive them here.
  // CONSEQUENCE, measured 2026-07-27 rather than assumed: scoring this corpus FROM INSIDE THIS REPOSITORY
  // reports 2 FN on this line and benchmark.mjs exits nonzero -- and not only on a fresh clone. The
  // analyzer honors .gitignore (crates/engine/src/pipeline/walking.rs), so recreating the file at this path
  // does NOT restore the score; the same corpus copied outside the repo, with the file present, scores
  // 143/143 clean. That is a harness state, not an engine result.
  // Since A17 (2026-08-03) this line legitimately carries THREE findings: the sk_live_ literal is a
  // digit-carrying vendor token (line-scan `hardcoded-secret` + `vendor-token-committed`, unchanged)
  // AND a 176-total-Shannon-bit value bound to `apiKey` — above `high-entropy-secret`'s measured
  // 80-bit floor, so the entropy rule co-fires by design (its message says so: the two rules read
  // different evidence and neither subsumes the other). Grow-only delta, adjudicated by reading the
  // anchored line.
  "api/services/be-security.hardcoded-secret.ts:3": ["security/hardcoded-secret","security/vendor-token-committed","security/high-entropy-secret"],
