  // ---- THE TWO NESTED PATH-SCOPE FIXTURES (added 2026-08-02) --------------------------------------
  // `sql/nplus1` scans only `.ts` under a `domains/<name>/routes/` or `api/` path SEGMENT. Until
  // 2026-08-01 its file_pattern was ROOT-anchored, so `src/api/orders.ts` was structurally invisible;
  // the fix aligned it to `(?:^|/)`, and the detection-gate delta of that fix was ZERO because all three
  // `api/` directories in this corpus sat at a tree root and no `domains/*/routes/` existed at all. These
  // two files are what makes the anchor regression-visible: re-root-anchor the pattern and both go red.
  // Adjudicated by reading the anchored line — each is the `await prisma.order.findMany(...)` inside the
  // `for` of that module's `bad` export, byte-identical to the root-level sibling at
  // `api/api/sql.nplus1.ts:8` whose verdict has been adjudicated since the file was rebuilt. Both modules
  // are ALSO registered in `trees/api-be/index.ts`; without that they are unimported orphans and pick up
  // `dead-candidates` + `unimported-export`, which was measured rather than assumed.
  "api/src/api/sql.nplus1-nested.ts:13": ["sql/nplus1"],
  "api/src/domains/orders/routes/sql.nplus1-domain.ts:10": ["sql/nplus1"],
  // ---- end nested path-scope fixtures ------------------------------------------------------------
