  ],

  // KNOWN CAPABILITY GAPS -- the third disposition (added 2026-07-29 together with the scorer support;
  // see the `gap` header in scripts/measure/benchmark.mjs). Same "<sourceId>/<path>:<line>": [ruleId]
  // shape as an expectation, and it means: THIS SHOULD FIRE ONCE A KNOWN CAPABILITY LANDS, AND TODAY IT
  // DOES NOT. Excluded from TP/FN/FP; counted and printed as `GAP n/N closed` in every run; exit-zero
  // while open; exit-NONZERO the day one fires, because that is progress to be promoted into an ordinary
  // expectation by hand and never absorbed. `scripts/detection-expected-baseline.txt` carries a third
  // column so an entry here cannot be quietly deleted -- a gap costs nothing in the score, so that column
  // is the only thing that would notice.
  //
  // THIS IS NOT A SUPPRESSION LIST. An entry earns its place by naming the capability, the code that
  // refuses it today, and what would close it. A FN with no named cause does not belong here; it belongs
  // in the score.
  //
  // EMPTY IS THE HEALTHY STATE, and it is empty right now. The two entries it held -- the consume side of
  // the unreadable-client-base shape, one per negative-case pair -- were closed by
  // `trees[].topology.clientBase` and promoted into ordinary expectations at
  // `feaxios/pages/articles.ts:39` and `fegensdk/api/Api.ts:20` (see the negative-case-pairs note above
  // for what that promotion cost and why the harness made it a hand edit). The disposition stays declared
  // rather than deleted because the next acknowledged gap should be written here, not re-invented.
  "gap": {},

  // Expectations anchored in files deliberately kept OUT of the tracked tree, as "<sourceId>/<path>"
  // (same shape as `benign`). benchmark.mjs reads this list and, when one of these produces a false
  // negative, prints WHY next to it -- so a fresh clone's red score cannot be misread as an engine
  // regression. The expectations stay in place and still count: the miss is real for whoever is running,
  // it just has a known non-engine cause. `.gitignore` is the authority on which files these are and why;
  // this list only names them so the score can point at that reason.
  "untracked": [
    "api/services/be-security.hardcoded-secret.ts"
  ]
}
